cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CL-DIY, please cite the accompanying paper (preprint link coming soon)."
title: "CL-DIY: Causal Loop? Do It Yourself!"
abstract: >-
  CL-DIY is an open-source, browser-based editor for building, exploring and
  refining causal loop diagrams. A diagram lives in a single self-contained
  HTML file that anyone can open in a web browser, with no installation, no
  account and no server. Users can edit variables and links, group variables
  into subsystems, trace and label feedback loops, and comment on each change,
  and can save their work as HTML, JSON or Vensim XMILE.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-20
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kajijoo/CL-DIY"
keywords:
  - causal loop diagrams
  - system dynamics
  - participatory modelling
  - group model building
